# WST Builder Plugin Package Boundary

Use this Rule when writing or reviewing reusable WST Builder plugin content.

The plugin package must be self-contained for consumers who only receive the `wst-builder` plugin folder. A required workflow step must not depend on files elsewhere in this development repository.

## Required Checks

- Every required Skill, Rule, reference, template, script, checklist, or workflow contract named by the plugin must exist inside the plugin package, which is `plugins/wst-builder` in this development repository, or be explicitly marked as an optional external dependency.
- Default WST Builder workflows must not require `.agents`, `.cursor/plugins/cache`, `weseo-smartflow-frontend-guide`, `.scratch`, repository-local scripts, or any other development-only path.
- If a workflow says "run `<skill-name>`", that Skill must be bundled in `plugins/wst-builder/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` unless the workflow clearly says the Skill is optional and external.
- The plugin README, manifest, release notes, rules, and skills must agree on the bundled content list.
- Manifest `source` fields and archive references are development provenance only. Runtime `path` fields and required workflow references must point to bundled plugin content.

Stop and fix the package before shipping if a required workflow path points outside the plugin folder.
